    <h2>Transfer in Slovenia </h2>

<p>Slovenia is a rather small country in Central Europe. Tourists often call Slovenia pastoral village, as it has almost no big cities. There are mostly tiny little provinces with one-story houses, and therefore transport infrastructure is not well developed. In the West, this small country has an access to the Adriatic sea. Most popular cities to visit are Ljubljana, Rogaska Slatina, Maribor, Bled.</p>

<p>Unfortunately, taxi service in Slovenia leaves much to be desired. Local drivers often try to cheat the client especially if they recognize you as a foreigner, who does not know the place well. In this case, they might choose a roundabout route or go on toll highways when it’s not necessary. But even if the driver is fair, you may have some difficulties as the language barrier is still there and the driver can simply misunderstand you.</p>

<p>It is rare to find a big taxi car in Slovenia as minibuses are not common. If you travel with a big group (of five people, for instance) it is possible that you won’t find a car of appropriate size, or if you will, it might take a lot of time. </p>

<p>You can easily avoid all those difficulties by ordering a transfer in Slovenia with online Kiwitaxi service. You can clearly see the cost of the needed route on the website in advance, and it will only depend on the car class, not on traffic, time of the day or luggage weight.</p>
  
<p>You can arrange the whole booking online at once and fully pay it by card, not to worry about money exchange whilst traveling. We will organize your transfer driver to meet you at the airport in Slovenia. He or she will have a sign with your name on it, help you with your luggage, and take you to any destination fast and safe without asking for any additional fees or tips. </p>
<p>Another important advantage: you will not face any translation problems as the driver will already know all the details of your trip and you will not have to explain anything. In case you have any questions, you can always ask for assistance from the English language support service 24/7. </p> 
<p>Transfers and taxis are a better solution than public transport: for example, traveling by bus in Slovenia can often be uncomfortable and inconvenient.</p>
